Publish curated release notes from tickets.

The GitHub release workflow currently uses automatically generated release notes. It should
instead publish curated Markdown stored in a ticket which has a `release-notes:<version>` metadata
item.

For a tag such as `v1.1.0`, the workflow should find exactly one ticket which has:

    release-notes: 1.1.0

The first description line is the ticket short description and should not be included in the
GitHub release body. All description content after that line should be copied without modification
to a Markdown notes file. Ticket comments after the next `---` separator should not be included.

The release must fail before publication when no matching ticket exists, more than one matching
ticket exists, or the extracted release body is empty.

The publish job should pass the extracted file to `gh release create` with `--notes-file` instead
of `--generate-notes`. Existing version validation, release title, assets, and tag verification
should remain unchanged.


Development Checklist:

